### Golden tests (next major deliverables)

**G0 — LOWG single-aerodrome VFR circuit-training golden** (active)
Single AI aircraft, parked at a LOWG stand, instructed to fly one VFR circuit
and return to the stand:
- Spawn at `LOWG_STAND_1` with `HighLevelGoal.CircuitTraining(circuits = 1, fullStopOnLast = true)`.
- One TOWER controller at 118.200 (per manifest — LOWG has no discrete GROUND
  or APPROACH; the tower handles all phases).
- `runUntil(...)` for ~30 sim minutes.
- Assertions: aircraft parked at the stand, altitude = 0, mission complete;
  expected instruction sequence on the wire; no looping geometry.

This is the test the LJMB-pivot replaced. The cross-aerodrome G1 below was
abandoned after a prolonged build-out delivered no flying. G0 is the first
test that will exercise `controllerDecide`'s 15-stage pipeline on real data.

Impact: H (the first end-to-end proof) | Effort: M (single airport, single role)

**G1 — Cross-aerodrome VFR round-trip LOWG ↔ LJMB** (deferred behind G0)
Originally scoped as the next golden; abandoned along with the speculative
cross-aerodrome production code (deletion captured in commit history). Will
return only once G0 is solid and there is concrete evidence the round-trip
test buys distinct coverage. Specifically: independent per-aerodrome
controllers, pilot-driven frequency changes on airspace boundaries, FIS
segment with no modelled controller, TMA/CTR entry corridors per Jepp 19-2.
The `MultiAerodromeWorldTest.kt` scaffold (real LOWG + LJMB merge, two
controllers, no flying) is retained as a thin smoke layer for if/when this
returns.

**REVIVAL (2026-05-16, fn-28.7):** the abandoned cross-aerodrome G1 surface
is partially revived as the **G3b sim golden**
(`sim/src/jvmTest/.../G3bCrossAerodromeReactiveTest.kt`). G3b composes G2's
single-direction LOWG → LJMB cross-aerodrome transit with a Transit-arrival
reactive-GA branch at LJMB (both crosswind and tailwind axes); the full
round-trip + FIS-segment + TMA-corridor surface remains deferred. The
revival lands the **first cross-aerodrome reactive-GA** path (seventh
reactive-GA path overall) — fn-28.6 widened `deriveCrosswindEvent` /
`deriveTailwindEvent` to a disjunctive eligibility (circuit OR Transit-
arrival) + extended `applyCrosswindGoAround` / `applyTailwindGoAround` with
a Transit dispatch fork via the shared `applyTransitArrivalReactiveGoAround`
helper using `replaceFromActivePrimitive([goAroundTask(), circuitTask(),
groundArrivalTask()])`. fn-28.7 closes
`D-PASS-g3b-react-cross-aerodrome-{crosswind,tailwind}` as the seventh +
eighth reactive-GA paths. The remaining round-trip / FIS / TMA work stays
deferred behind concrete coverage evidence.

Impact: H | Effort: H

